ses the victim to harassment and  shame  and the whole thing it must be taken  seriously when a victim  makes an allegation this is simply about  all that i'm talking about now  is that there could not possibly be  based on everything we know right now  a conclusive investigation there's a  bigger topic as well which is  can someone prove they did not commit a  sexual assault when the allegations  themselves are like the ones we have  here  there's only a very narrow way that you  could prove you did not commit a sexual  assault and that would be  like imagine that tara reid filed a  complaint on a specific day  and we saw oh the allegation is that  this supposedly took place on this day  and then biden's travel schedule  from that time shows he was out of the  country  okay maybe in that narrow scenario you  could conclude he didn't do it  but beyond that you can't really prove  you didn't commit sexual assault and in  this particular case  we can't even find the complaint biden  said release certain records but he  hasn't said release others  tara reid doesn't have a copy of the  complaint she previously said the  complaint was for sexual assault now she  says the complaint she did file  doesn't mention sexual assault but it  describes sexual harassment  but there's no copy of the complaint so  what i am telling you is  not that she's telling the truth or that  she's lying we should take her  allegations seriously  but there is not a complaint to  investigate joe biden cannot prove his  innocence nor is there any way to  confirm tara reid's allegations  there couldn't be a conclusive  investigation now what about this idea  that's floating around that  she was fired because of the complaint  that she filed  it's such a mess at this point that no  investigation could conclude  anything she says she was fired for  filing the complaint we can't find  there's a negative performance review on  file whose timing can be used to call  this into question well  what if you 